        "sentence_id": "e47e032153907da7362e2d6d77e0f63f",
        "sentence_text": " After the Act of Union 1800, Ireland was part of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland, whose Parliament passed the Weights and Measures Act 1824, which established English measure in Ireland as \"Imperial measure\" or \"statute measure\".",
        "sentence_token_cost": 57,
